  "release_scope": "Mac stable + separate Dev distribution and iPad stable device release, paired to the same shared userspace Linux runtime",
  "release_fixes": [
    "Accepted exec ELF jobs remain externally live after a worker cohort returns. Existing disk completion unparks the original driver; no new coordinator, worker-service or ordinary syscall/instruction check.",
    "Proc fdinfo can observe its own original OFD without recursively locking its active offset transaction. Mutations and pending-read counts retain the original object mutex; a committed relaxed-atomic scalar supplies metadata observations without stronger guest memory order.",
    "Mac managed start/restart requires a connectable console listener, rather than a stale socket pathname. Existing startup lock/deadline are retained; no guest hot path is involved.",
    "A test-only Memory cache assertion now permits legitimate invalidation when unrelated tests advance the global backing revision. Original physical alias, code epoch and byte visibility assertions remain unconditional; production Memory code is unchanged."
  ],
